cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its reported results, please cite this repository and record the commit used."
type: software
title: "FAM-Jet: exact temporal moments for deferred memory queries"
authors:
  - family-names: Legotin
    given-names: Artem
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-25"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arlegotin/FAM-Jet"
url: "https://github.com/arlegotin/FAM-Jet"
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Local research software for query-conditioned associative memory with exact
  dimensionless first temporal moments. Includes streaming and terminal
  implementations, direct references, byte-matched exponential-bank and
  storage baselines, fixed-writer query-conditioned ridge readers, protected
  synthetic confirmation and independent replication, chronological Beijing
  PM2.5 transfer, cost accounting and sealed report replay. Both synthetic
  panels have 3072 histories and favor Jet in point estimate, but both paired
  conditional intervals include zero. Temporal buckets have lower average
  synthetic loss; the real-trained ordinary bank has lower sensor RMSE.
  No overall Jet advantage, architecture novelty, all-family superiority or
  language/agent-memory result is established. Original failures and the
  separate report-only recovery provenance are retained.
keywords:
  - streaming memory
  - temporal queries
  - exponential moments
  - bounded memory
  - reproducible research
  - negative results
